{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935925-so-you-ve-captured-a-seer-now-what","id":935925,"title":"So You've Captured a Seer, Now What?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-22T21:18:50-07:00","id":935925,"title":"So You've Captured a Seer, Now What?","content":"If a pentacle cabal captures a seer what should they do?<br /> <br /> The answer probably depends on what the circumstances were so I'll break it down by categories.<br /> <br /> It was an accident: The cabal cast a sleep spell (or other incapacitating spell) on a large area for an unrelated purpose and discover they accidentally caught a seer.<br /> <br /> They were provoked: A seer attacked them and they won.<br /> <br /> It was a misunderstanding: The cabal was embedded in a fight between sleepers for some reason, and incapacitated a seer who was on the other side.<br /> <br /> Side question: if you realize there is another mage (pentacle or seer) on an opposing side in a battle mostly consisting of sleepers what do you do.<br /> <br /> I'm curious what people think because I am planning an unusual chronicle where these situations might come up a few times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T21:31:06-07:00","id":935929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935925-so-you-ve-captured-a-seer-now-what#post935925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a pentacle cabal captures a seer what should they do?<br /> <br /> The answer probably depends on what the circumstances were so I'll break it down by categories.<br /> <br /> It was an accident: The cabal cast a sleep spell (or other incapacitating spell) on a large area for an unrelated purpose and discover they accidentally caught a seer.<br /> <br /> They were provoked: A seer attacked them and they won.<br /> <br /> It was a misunderstanding: The cabal was embedded in a fight between sleepers for some reason, and incapacitated a seer who was on the other side.<br /> <br /> Side question: if you realize there is another mage (pentacle or seer) on an opposing side in a battle mostly consisting of sleepers what do you do.<br /> <br /> I'm curious what people think because I am planning an unusual chronicle where these situations might come up a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's all that unusual. Your players have to be creative in the ways they handle these situations. That's part of the horror. I have a story of my PCs unexpectedly and horrifically torturing a Sleeper for info on a mission they had undertaken. A Sleeper who didn't know anything at all (not that the other way would have excused it).<br /> <br /> Mages are not superheroes. This is a horror game. Don't get rid of it. Embrace it. Start fights with a lot of Sleepers around, make it so that they can't default to magic with so many Reaches.<br /> <br /> (And the answer to the first question depends a lot on the context, so I'm afraid I don't have an answer for you there.<br /> <br /> But embrace the horror. That's my advice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T03:06:06-07:00","id":936004,"title":"","content":"Blank the time they spent in custody with Mind/Time or forbid them from speaking about it with Fate. Steal their stuff and inflict curses of PCs' choice. Mandate that they create a soul stone, keep the stone, and send them on their way, possibly attempting to trade for any Pentacle prisoners the local Seers have.<br /> <br /> Page 98: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Orders (even the Seers) have a simple method for resolving conflicts when one mage has possession of another\u2019s soul stone against his will. The stone must be returned after the creator performs three services for the holder. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T11:01:44-07:00","id":936158,"title":"","content":"I hate to say it, but how a cabal reacts to a Seer should depend on context. You've given us some, but there's more required.<br /> <br /> Something to remember as a background context is that there is theory and practice and the two are distinctly different. In theory, Seers and the Pentacle are in a state of constant war with one another and enemies to the end; the only good Seer is a dead Seer. A good Atlantean (or libertine) gets as much information and as many resources out of a Seer captive as possible before disposing of them in a timely, efficient, and clean manner, free of sadism and cruelty.<br /> <br /> Practice isn't theory, though. The war between the two sides is very real and shaped by circumstance. How a Seer is captured generally matters less than the context they were captured in, but not entirely.<br /> <br /> If the local Atlanteans are more powerful than the local Seers to a significant degree (i.e. outnumbering the Seers 10 to 1 and with far more powerful elders), the Atlanteans may have carte blanche to do with the Seer captive as they see fit. They're an enemy of the Awakened Nation and not a part of the local Consilium, so the local law probably says you can hang them from a meat hook if you want to. Every Seer is a potential murderer and possibly an in-fact murderer. Torture is still frowned upon when done without purpose, but, in the end, they're a literal insurgent faction; few people are going to rake you over the coals and fewer still are going to investigate in the first place.<br /> <br /> If the Seers are more potent, though, there's political nuance to be considered. Any act taken against the Seers <i>will</i> have consequences. If you took a captive as a part of an ongoing campaign, that's fine; it probably falls under the same category as above, though you may be expected to share what you find with the Consilium at large. If you took them captive as a part of a dispute known and recognized between two specific sub-groups of each faction, you'll be expected to act with honour and decorum; fighting <i>only</i> to get what the dispute was about. If it's to the death, it's to the death, but if it isn't, killing them will be bad for you. There might even be formal agreements specifically for sorting out this sort of thing between the local Pylon(s) and Consilium.<br /> <br /> And if the Seers are more powerful, well... Capturing someone is bad for you and killing them's worse. Being noticed at all is a bad thing. Then it's more of a hostage situation; releasing them only - <i>only</i> - when you have Fate-bound oaths, sworn on their part in the name of the Exarchs, to let you be. Or, if you're the insurgent faction now, you use them to drive as many long knives into as many Seers as possible, because, no matter what you do, a bunch are about to be turned on you. Get gone.<br /> <br /> And then you have the personal context. What do the characters want? And who is this Seer to them? Young characters are probably the most eager to put a dagger in them for the Atlantean cause but the least likely to do so. Older characters, who recognize political nuance, are more likely to have lost friends, maybe even family, to the Seer cause and seen just what the Seers are really like. The more experienced they are, the more likely they are to realize killing is a bad idea, but also the more likely they are to want to do so.<br /> <br /> So, tl;dr: What will the political repercussions be of any given action and how much do the characters want to make the captive bleed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T12:08:02-07:00","id":936181,"title":"","content":"This actually came up in the Man Comes Around, the players caught a Banisher and his prisoner, they were ordered to kill the Banisher, but only strongly recommended to kill the prisoner who turned out to be a Seer. They decided that killing the Banisher had been necessary as he was a direct risk to them, but killing the Seer would have been more a matter of necessity than convenience. So with his cooperation (He didn't want to die, obviously) they dived into his Oneiros and obscured his memories of them. Later in the chronicle this decision comes back to bite them in the ass. Anyway, point is, it can go any way the players want really and is highly context dependent like Axelgear said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:29:51-07:00","id":938130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're an enemy of the Awakened Nation and not a part of the local Consilium, so the local law probably says you can hang them from a meat hook if you want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Awakened are one nation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:54:21-07:00","id":938152,"title":"","content":"Indeed. That's what makes it so awful: It's treason, not invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:38:45-07:00","id":938392,"title":"","content":"I think he was hitting at something different;<br /> Consider it like this - for many Mages, belonging to one of the sects is like...well...belonging to a club, religion, whatever organization; you either are one of them by following their rules, or you don't and you are not. If you are a sinner, you might get removed from the society, or be refused certain services (example: certain politicians might be refused holy communion if they publicly support something considered to be a sin).<br /> So if you are a Seer, a Nameless, or an Apostate? We are not obliged to extend our services to you, we don't have to protect you, and if you are one of us, you may say &quot;I'm not anymore&quot; and lose all of your benefits.<br /> <br /> Silver Ladder doesn't think like that.<br /> They consider all Awakened to be One Nation. Nation has certain obligations towards it's citizens. Even if they don't pay taxes, try to become independent, or murder people, they are still citizens of that nation, and that nation has to respect these rights, these obligations. From Nation's point of view, you can't quit being a citizen by yelling loudly, and even if you do, as it's member there are things it simply cannot stop, even if you don't want them.<br /> So for a Adamantine Arrow, that Seer is an outsider, someone who isn't one of us, and thus can be punched, even if we don't punch others of our kind.<br /> For a Silver Ladder, that Seer is <i>still one of ours, and we still have our obligations towards him.*</i><br /> <br /> This is probably why Consilia don't devolve into tyrannical oligarchies based on pure Strong Beats The Weak.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> So, a very simplified and shallow read, but:<br /> For Arrows, Seers are rivals. Rivals are to be defeated.<br /> For Guardians, Seers are dangerous neighbours. These are to be kept in check and outsmarted, sometimes - cooperated with.<br /> For Mysterium...Iit's too complicated.<br /> For Free Council, they are enemies. Not rivals. Enemies. Enemies are to be DESTROYED.<br /> For Silver Ladder, they are misguided faction. They are to be integrated.<br /> <br /> *This is, of course, sneaky. They assume that, by default, you are One Nation, and thus, have to follow One Nation's Laws. So for Silver Ladder? Every Mage should follow Lex Magica, and they are not allowed to disagree. A Ladder-Centric Consilium would probably enforce it's laws even on those who aren't members, because <i>they decided that all are members.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-27-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:57:24-07:00","id":938407,"title":"","content":"I was basing a lot of what I said on those same justifications: A foreigner follows foreign laws; they are not bound to your rules. Citizens of the same nation are obligated to follow the same laws.<br /> <br /> If the Awakened are one nation, being a Seer doesn't mean you're just disagreeing; it means you are a seditious and treasonous traitor. Whatever rights you had were curtailed by your choice to rebel, as they are with all criminals. Enemies of unity can, nay, must be converted or destroyed. <br /> <br /> Thearchs might wish to convert Seers in theory, but they'd also like to do the same with Banishers and Scelesti. In practice, the conversion is usually more from 'person' to 'corpse'.<br /> <br /> Edit: It is worth adding that they probably have a right to a trial in many dominions, but in most places, I imagine that only applies to Consilium members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 07-27-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:29:08-07:00","id":938926,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd like to go Bastila Shan and slap the Seer with Psychic Reprogramming. Unless they're a Prelate in which case Tranform Life, teeth to the throat.<br /> <br /> Follower of the Lie, destroyed.<br /> <br /> Of course, I personally am likely to have Mind as Inferiour, so I'd have to ask a Mind Adept to do it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:03:27-07:00","id":939064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935925-so-you-ve-captured-a-seer-now-what?p=938926#post938926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like to go Bastila Shan and slap the Seer with Psychic Reprogramming. Unless they're a Prelate in which case Tranform Life, teeth to the throat.<br /> <br /> Follower of the Lie, destroyed.<br /> <br /> Of course, I personally am likely to have Mind as Inferiour, so I'd have to ask a Mind Adept to do it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, would see such a fate as worse than death. The mage society as a whole would probably have similar opinion. Not only is it risky in the longer run, but by using mind control in such a way, you would serve the Exarchs better the the Seers themselves do. You would \u0336f\u0336a\u0336l\u0336l\u0336 \u0336t\u0336o\u0336 \u0336t\u0336h\u0336e\u0336 \u0336d\u0336a\u0336r\u0336k\u0336 \u0336s\u0336i\u0336d\u0336e\u0336 be on a good way to become a Seer yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:23:57-07:00","id":939078,"title":"","content":"Not just Seers use Psychic Reprogramming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:49:45-07:00","id":939106,"title":"","content":"The idea is that you would strenghten the symbols of control over mankind (Exarchs) by using reprogramming in such an indiscriminate way. You might not call yourself a Seer, but your mentality would sure be close to the Seer worldview. If you decided to &quot;solve&quot; your problems by fucking with people's minds in such a brutal manner, you would be a Seer in anything but name.<br /> <br /> It has been some time since I've red it, but I believe that Dave's Soul Cage AP actually has this situation come up with one of the characters and the General.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 07-28-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:24:54-07:00","id":939131,"title":"","content":"Who said it's indiscriminate or that it's done brutally? I think Tambov's view of Seers is overly-simplistic, but I find your knee-jerk reaction to Psychic Reprogramming to be similarly limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-28-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:41:29-07:00","id":939148,"title":"","content":"Sure, you don't have to torture the Seer or cause the pain by less physical means, but a wholecloth change of personality Revan-style can be classified as essentially similar to murder + potential mental baggage for the new personality if the spell is less than perfect. The original person is gone and might as well be dead.<br /> <br /> Some of the definitions of the word brutal are 'harsh' and 'inhuman'. Pushing your desires onto other previously sovereign minds so that they become puppets to your desires and goals, whether by creating those desires on a moments' notice, or by substituting an entire personality acting in line with your agenda seems pretty inhuman to me. That's also why it's a Wisdom sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 07-28-2016, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:15:52-07:00","id":939177,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm actually a bit with Prometheus here. Even if I don't believe mental content is synonymous with identity, that wholesale transformation of a person - an erasure of their deepest beliefs and the rewriting of the very core of their self - is a horrible violation, and one that is terrible to use even in morally justifiable scenarios.<br /> <br /> You're putting a mental slave collar on them; you are degrading and eliminating their most basic humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:40:41-07:00","id":939191,"title":"","content":"The Mind arcana can be very subtle, you really don't need to do the KOTOR style total rewrite unless they're a Prelate or something, in which case, there's probably some greater reason you're doing it.<br /> <br /> As a start you could use Read the Depths to actually see how deeply committed the Seer is. You might not even need magic to persuade them after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:18:53-07:00","id":939306,"title":"","content":"Nothing to see here; move along, citizen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxp